<!--
  The launcher mark: a shield with the browser's arrow cut clean through it.

  Two things about it are deliberate.

  The arrow is a *hole*, not a second shape. `fillType="evenOdd"` makes the
  inner subpath subtract from the outer one, so the whole mark is a single
  solid colour and the arrow shows whatever is behind it. That is what lets one
  path serve as the launcher foreground (over the blue gradient), as the
  monochrome layer (over whatever colour Android 13 themes it) and as the brand
  mark on the sign-in screen, without three versions drifting apart.

  Everything sits inside the 66 × 66 safe zone of the 108 × 108 adaptive-icon
  canvas. An adaptive icon is masked to whatever shape the launcher wants, and
  anything outside that circle-and-a-bit is not guaranteed to survive the crop.

  The shield is the app's one idea — uBlock always on, VPN a tap away — and the
  same motif the menu, the settings rows and the VPN screen already carry. It is
  drawn at icon scale rather than reusing ic_shield's 24dp path: that one is a
  20-pixel glyph and its proportions do not survive being blown up to 108.
  This replaces a placeholder "U" that had been sitting here since the first
  commit.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M54,26 L80,35 L80,54 C80,68.5 69.6,80.4 54,86 C38.4,80.4 28,68.5 28,54 L28,35 Z M54,37 L69,55 L60.5,55 L60.5,75 L47.5,75 L47.5,55 L39,55 Z" />
</vector>
